> > cloning a monster doesn't bump the counter.
> 
> Is that a feature, to enable pudding farming, or a bug,
> because it uses a path where the counter update was
> forgotten, or doesn't the code give enough hints to
> let you guess either way?

There used to be a comment in the extinction code that "[counter
bumping] requires that the caller manually decrement mvitals if the
monster is created under circumstances where one would not logically
expect the creation to reduce the supply of wild monsters. Monster
cloning might be one such case, but we go against logic there in order
to reduce the possibility of abuse." I pointed out to the DevTeam that
cloning _didn't_ in fact go against that logic; it respects extinction
but does not contribute to it, since it doesn't call that code at
all. They changed the comment to read "Monster cloning might be one
case that requires that in order to reduce the possibility of abuse,
but currently doesn't." (The comment has vanished entirely in 3.4.3,
when extinction-tracking was made into its own function.)

This progression indicates to me that the "possibility of abuse"
isn't currently seen as requiring limiting.

